        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3\\sqrt3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}AX&=AB-XB\\\\AX&=5\\sqrt3-2\\sqrt3\\\\AX&=3\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$AY$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4\\sqrt2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}AY^2&=AX^2+YX^2\\\\AY^2&=(3\\sqrt3)^2+(\\sqrt5)^2\\\\AY^2&=27+5\\\\AY&=\\sqrt{32}\\\\AY&=4\\sqrt2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$CZ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{2\\sqrt5}{3}$",
          "worked": "Since $XY ZB$ forms a rectangle, $BZ=YX=\\sqrt5$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}CZ&=CB-BZ\\\\CZ&=\\frac{5\\sqrt5}{3}-\\sqrt5\\\\CZ&=\\frac{2\\sqrt5}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$YC$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{8\\sqrt2}{3}$",
          "worked": "Opposite sides of the rectangle give $YZ=XB=2\\sqrt3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}YC^2&=YZ^2+CZ^2\\\\YC^2&=(2\\sqrt3)^2+\\left(\\frac{2\\sqrt5}{3}\\right)^2\\\\YC^2&=12+\\frac{20}{9}\\\\YC^2&=\\frac{128}{9}\\\\YC&=\\frac{\\sqrt{128}}3\\\\YC&=\\frac{8\\sqrt2}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 72
      }
